    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0099" n="3" xml:id="pg3"/>

                <head>No. 3.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">To the consuls-general, consuls, and
                        commercial agents of the United States in Europe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 3,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: In view of representations made to
                    the Department, it is deemed desirable that the next annual report of consular
                    officers in Europe should contain a table showing the humidity of each month of
                    the year at those places within their respective districts where meteorological
                    observations are taken. For the purposes of these reports the year will be
                    understood to be the fiscal year.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, vour obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. W. SEWARD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
